(Background: Despite distribution of insecticide-treated nets, malaria transmission) Tj
T*
(persists in sub-Saharan Africa due to insecticide resistance and outdoor biting. Spatial) Tj
T*
(repellents offer a complementary approach. This study protocol outlines a cluster-) Tj
T*
(randomized trial evaluating a novel transfluthrin-based spatial repellent product.) Tj
T*
(Methods: The trial will be conducted in rural Kenya across matched clusters of households) Tj
T*
(with children aged 6 months to 10 years. Clusters are randomly assigned to receive the) Tj
T*
(novel spatial repellent product or standard prevention guidance. The intervention involves) Tj
T*
(monthly product installation and replacement. Primary efficacy outcome: malaria infection) Tj
